    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0293" n="183" xml:id="pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2037: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Nanking</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-13T15:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>91. For the Minister: Legation’s 740, October 10 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >11</hi>], 8 a.m. In view of your 748, October 12, 8 p.m., you are authorized in
                    reply to inform the Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs that the American
                    Government is expecting momentarily to receive from American official sources a
                    full report with regard to the incident at Chinchow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
